From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:39:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Publish DRAPS stats straight to the weekly approval tab

Publish now writes one row per rep per day to "Rep DRAPS - For Approval"
in the weekly report sheet (WEEKLY_SHEET_ID), so the weekly sheet no longer
has to load stats from the DRAPS Log. The DRAPS Log and rep list are unchanged.

- lib/approval.js maps DRAPS fields to approval columns A to Y. Super and
  RE-FI are blank, since DRAPS has no fields for them.
- Notes to the right of column Y are left alone on republish.
- Logged At is Brisbane time, DD/MM/YYYY HH:mm.
- New env var WEEKLY_SHEET_ID; SHEET_ID still points at the DRAPS sheet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
